epochs, which was the minimum among the four methods, indicating that Adam optimizer can improve the global optimization ability of the compensation algorithm. The minimum MSE of the four combinations of activation functions and optimizers were compared in Table 2, which clearly seen the advantage of Softplus activation function combined with Adam optimizer on MSE. The compensation results of this improved deep BP neural network were shown in Table 3. The predicted concentrations of NO2 were remarkably close to the actual concentrations. And the relative error was less than 1.37%, which is defined as (predicted concentration–actual concentration)/actual concentration* 100%. The recognition accuracy of this model structure with optimization algorithms under the same temperature or humidity conditions were studied as well. The samples at 40 ◦C or 50% RH were chosen as the development set, respectively. For the training set with constant humidity conditions, MSE reached to about 0.0164 after 40,146 epochs, with a relative error of less than 2.07% (Fig. S4a, S4b and Table S2). For the training set with constant temperature conditions, after 21,026 times of training, MSE was about 0.0110, with a relative error of less than 1.45% (Fig. S4c, S4d and Table S3). The lack of randomness, as well as the reduced training set, mainly resulted in increased MSE. But the high recognition accuracies were still kept. In the actual agricultural environment, temperature and humidity change constantly, so this designed model can well ensure the gas sensor to achieve high accuracy. The recognition ability of the model was further verified through the obtained sampling data from the commercial NO2 sensor (taking 20 ◦C,
35 ◦C, 40 ◦C and 45 ◦C as example). The proportion of training test set was increased to 20%, which further avoided the phenomenon of over fitting. The batch-size was set to 68. After 1214 epochs, MSE was about 0.0101, with a relative error of less than 1.42% (Fig. S5a, S5b and Table S4). The increased MSE was mainly attributed to the lack of obvious changing pattern of voltage especially at high humidity [31], as well as the huge amount of data for the test set [32]. However, because of the huge development set, the number of training rounds was greatly reduced, and the speed of convergence to the global optimum was significantly increased, compared with PbS based NO2 sensor. Although the MSE was a little increased, the model showed high recognition accuracy, proving the excellent generalization ability again, whether applied for the fabricated chemical sensors or commercial electrochemical sensors. This excellent generalization ability of this improved BP neural network was derived from its strong self-learning and self-adaptability. In particular, the model can accurately predict the NO2 concentration under any temperature and humidity condition, showing the good environmental adaptability. The compensation performance of the improved deep BP neural network was compared with the existing reports, as shown in Table 4. Our constructed model obtained the smallest relative error among the existing methods.
4. Conclusion
An improved deep BP neural network with low MSE and relative error was developed to enhance the accuracy of NO2 sensor applied in complex temperature and humidity environments. Totally 240 sample data were acquired by the fabricated PbS nanoparticles based NO2 sensor under different conditions. A 14-layer deep BP neural network model was constructed, and two strategies were proposed to obtain the low MSE and high accuracy of the model. First, SGD algorithm with Mini-batch was chosen to balance the model performance and the training time complexity. Mini-batch algorithm can take the advantages of the parallel computing ability of the CPU or GPU and the optimization ability of the SGD algorithm simultaneously, thereby accelerating the training speed on the basis of ensuring the training performance. Second, Softplus activation function combined with Adam optimizer was selected to reduce the MSE and obtain accurate recognized results of NO2 concentrations. Based on the synergy of the unsaturation of Softplus function and the high computational efficiency of Adam optimizer, the
